    "intro_narrative": "The world ended not with a bang, but with a sudden, silent digital collapse. You are a Scavenger exploring the ruins of Outpost 31, a legendary pre-collapse bunker rumored to hold the 'Genesis Code'—humanity's last chance to restore the biosphere. The bunker is a tangled mess of interconnected mainframes, biometric locks, and archaic processors. The air is thick with dust, and the only light comes from the faint amber glow of surviving command terminals. Your objective is clear: navigate this labyrinth of forgotten technology, restore the power flow between the core systems, and ultimately unlock the final cache containing the Genesis Code. The systems here are heavily interdependent. You'll need to trace the physical and digital paths, bringing offline systems back to life one by one. Time is running out as the bunker's backup generators begin to fail. Connect the right modules, synthesize the necessary tools, and unravel the post-apocalyptic web to secure the future.",
    "narrative_style": "post_apocalyptic"
